ladies and gentlemen distinguished  guests  dear friends welcome to the 14th edition  of the european development days  this year's meeting on the green deal  for sustainable future  could not come at a more crucial time  the covet 19 pandemic has just  shown us how directly the health of our  people  and the health of our planet are  interconnected  of course it was already clear prior to  the pandemic  that climate change is the defining  challenge of our time  it therefore was a top priority for our  commission from day one  with our european green deal we want to  lead the way  for green and inclusive transformation  of our economies and our societies  and the pandemic has made this task even  more urgent  we have spoken a lot about the link  between  biodiversity loss and covet 19.  now we must move to action  and this is why just recently at the  global health summit  the commission together with the italian  g20 presidency  put the one health approach  in the center of the rome declaration  also economically this is the right  thing to do  the harm that we are doing to the earth  climate and environment is also harming  the well-being of  billions of people worldwide and this is  why it is right and also prudent  to invest quickly and boldly in the  health of our planet  this year's edition of the european  development days  takes place as we prepare the road to  the un  biodiversity conference in kunming  there we want to agree on a powerful new  global biodiversity framework  a framework that mobilizes all citizens  and all parts of government and society  and i'm sure these european development  days  will build momentum towards kunming  with more than 170 organizations from  across the world  this exchange of youth will be a truly  global one  and the next two days are a unique  opportunity to share ideas and to share  experiences  and it will help to inspire new  partnerships  and of course to find innovative  solutions  the development days are not only about  ideas  but also about action the european union  is ready to work with partners to  address both  the biodiversity loss and the climate  crisis  that's why the european union is working  towards global commitments  to protect 30 percent of our land and  our sea this is a goal for the  biodiversity cup  15 in china and we are also  aiming to increase climate ambitions  in glasgow the european union is  determined to turn these challenges  into economic opportunities the question  how to ensure green growth will be key  to speed up global efforts against  climate change  and the loss of biodiversity we as a  european union we want to lead the way  when the answers are formulated in  kunming  and dear friends we have seen our young  generation  taking to the streets they are standing  up and putting the planet's health first  and rightly so because their future is  at stake  their voices must have a significant  impact  on our policies and actions and  therefore i am delighted  that we have a remarkable group of  talented young leaders  with us in this opening ceremony  this year we want young people to shape  the discussion  and beyond this i know that commissioner  yota orpilin's  youth sounding board initiative will  open new possibilities  to hear directly from young people  we need you we need the young with your  energy  your drive and your vision to take on  the huge challenge facing your  generation  because we all know it will take courage  leadership and political will to push  for the greater good  but it is worth any effort and you can  count on europe  so let's get started
 

